= Authorization — Technical =

Authorization mechanisms include access-control lists, role-based access control, attribute-based access control, relationship-based models, and capabilities. The policy decision point can be separated from enforcement, identity, and resource services.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* authorization ≠ authentication
* authorization ≠ identity
* access decision ≠ proof of legitimacy outside the policy

== References ==
* NIST SP 800-162, ''Guide to Attribute Based Access Control (ABAC) Definition and Considerations'' (2014).
* NIST RBAC literature and ANSI INCITS 359 role-based access-control standard family.
* NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5, access-control control family.
